    I doubt that there is a lot to be gained, because we typically keep quorum connections open for a long time and don't create new sockets frequently. I think it only happens when the leader changes or an offline node comes back online.

    Also, is the factory thread-safe? You can only cache it if so. If it's not, then every thread would need its own and at that point it may not be worth it.
