    I got a little confused with ClientX509Util/QuorumX509Util classes. Looks like we don't use `ClientX509Util` to setup the pipeline for ZooKeeper client connections, it's essentially only used in the quorum communication for server and client side of server-server connections.

    In which case I agree with caching the `SocketFactory` would not give noticeable performance gain. 

    I'm also wondering whether it makes sense to move the SSLEngine setup logic in `InitSSL()` of `NettyServerCnxnFactory` to ClientX509Util. 
;11/Jun/18 13:33;githubbot;600

