    I'm struggling to get this right, so really curious about your implementation. The SSL side works fine, I can create the special socket combined with the InputStream as suggested to channel back already consumed data, but how can I do the same with non-SSL socket?

    Modified `UnifiedServerSocket` like this:
    ```java
            final Socket normalSocket = new Socket();
            implAccept(normalSocket);

            byte[] litmus = new byte[5];
            int bytesRead = normalSocket.getInputStream().read(litmus, 0, 5);

            if (bytesRead == 5 && SslHandler.isEncrypted(ChannelBuffers.wrappedBuffer(litmus))) {
                LOG.info(getInetAddress() + " attempting to connect over ssl");
                SSLSocket sslSocket;
                try {
                    sslSocket = x509Util.createSSLSocket(normalSocket, new ByteArrayInputStream(litmus));
                } catch (X509Exception e) {
                    throw new IOException("failed to create SSL context", e);
                }
                sslSocket.setUseClientMode(false);
                return sslSocket;
            } else {
                LOG.info(getInetAddress() + " attempting to connect without ssl");
                return normalSocket;
            }
    ```
    Last return statement lacks of channeling back the litmus, hence it cannot be read on server side.
;14/Jun/18 20:54;githubbot;600

