    the local variable `sslServerHostnameVerificationEnabled` is read from the config option `getSslHostnameVerificationEnabledProperty` - the config option is not server-specific. So I think the confusion is from local variable naming. Change it to something like:

      boolean hostnameVerificationEnabled = config.getBoolean(this.getSslHostnameVerificationEnabledProperty(), true);
      // If hostname verification is enabled, we always verify servers
      boolean sslServerHostnameVerificationEnabled = hostnameVerificationEnabled;
      // We verify clients only if hostname verification is enabled in the config,
      // and `shouldVerifyClientHostname()` returns true.
      boolean sslClientHostnameVerificationEnabled = shouldVerifyClientHostname() && hostnameVerificationEnabled;
;02/Oct/18 21:05;githubbot;600

