23/Oct/07 17:36;mbrown;I just benchmarked getline() from stdcxx 4.1.3 against the same function in gcc 4.1 (the program is below), and out of curiosity against the wc utility on Linux. stdcxx is more than twice slower than gcc, and nearly ten times slower than wc.The timings for a 32MB text file are:

$ ls -l input.txt && time LD_LIBRARY_PATH=../lib ./getline 1 input.txt && time ./a.out 1 input.txt && time wc -l input.txt && cat getline.cpp
